Guard the hm-session-vars.sh source in home-manager's generic-linux target.

Upstream unconditionally sources hm-session-vars.sh in programs.bash.initExtra.
That ~/.bashrc is bind-mounted into dctl devcontainers, which never run Home
Manager, so the file is absent there and the source errors at shell start. This
adds an `[ -f ] &&` guard: a no-op on the host (file present), silent in
containers. See nix-config/modules/home/generic-linux.nix.

If a home-manager bump changes this line, this patch fails LOUDLY at eval — re-sync it then.

--- a/generic-linux.nix
+++ b/generic-linux.nix
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
     # https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/pull/797#issuecomment-544783247
     programs.bash.initExtra = ''
       . "${nixPkg}/etc/profile.d/nix.sh"
-      . "${profileDirectory}/etc/profile.d/hm-session-vars.sh"
+      [ -f "${profileDirectory}/etc/profile.d/hm-session-vars.sh" ] && . "${profileDirectory}/etc/profile.d/hm-session-vars.sh"
     '';

     programs.zsh.envExtra = ''
